- *Registered verdict:* "nothing resolved above the anchors: undecided".
- *Descriptive reading (not registered):* the committed records fix the
  closure degree at 4 for m·ℓ ≤ 18 and above 4 at m·ℓ = 21, so the local
  slope over 18–21 is at least 0.33; a fitted slope below 0.10 would need
  the degree to hold at 5 to about m·ℓ = 28, below 0.03 to about 51. Both
  are consistent with the data and untested by it.
- *Feasibility wall (measured):* at N = 40 the sparse closure caps at
  350 M entries in about 3 minutes at degrees 5 and 6; F4 (a probe, not
  registered) was stopped by its 1 GiB step-matrix cap and, with the cap
  raised, killed at 12.6 GB RSS in the degree-5 step. At N = 46 even degree
  4 caps after 8,466 s.
- *Soundness control:* none run here (see P5); the sparse engine rests on
  its agreement test with the dense closure and on P4.
- *Scope:* every statement is about m·ℓ ≤ 24 on this 4-core, 15 GB host.

